-- MediFlow: synthetic outpatient demonstration database snapshot
-- Generated at UTC: 2026-10-24T15:38:36.788138+00:00
-- Repository commit: 64a1f04340efe07d324a1335d44c2b90baac68fd
-- Format: PostgreSQL plain SQL with psql meta-commands; eight separate databases.
-- Schema, application data and Flyway history are included. No global roles/role passwords or ownership/ACL commands are exported.
-- Account password hashes are necessary application data; plaintext login credentials are not embedded in this header/manifest.
-- Run with psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -d postgres -f <this-file> on an isolated target.
-- Do not use psql --single-transaction: CREATE DATABASE and multi-database connections require separate transactions.
-- All eight targets are checked before any application schema or data is loaded.
-- An existing public table causes an explicit error. No existing business data is removed.
-- Restore is not atomic across databases: after a mid-restore failure, use a new empty isolated target.
-- Lab correction 2026-10-24: only documentation comments updated; original schema/data/audit remain unchanged.
-- See LAB-NORMAL-VERIFICATION.md and Run-LabNormalAcceptance.ps1 beside this dump.
-- Follow-up 2026-10-25: full eight-context restore and populated-target refusal rehearsed;
-- see FOLLOWUP-VERIFICATION.md for six-deployment and client smoke (not every workflow).
-- Billing V1 lifecycle listener correction is in the same patch branch; rebuild Billing too.
-- Do not set clearance_target_id=test_id or reset inbox/outbox to prepare the demo.
-- Patched Lab also restores exact grant instants from its immutable inbox; keep original raw_body bytes intact.
-- Limitations:
--   - Synthetic outpatient demo only; Inpatient and Surgery databases are excluded.
--   - A finite set of recorded scenarios is not proof that every workflow or failure case passes.
--   - RabbitMQ queue contents, process clocks, service configuration, feature gates and pricing configuration are not included.
--   - Application outbox/inbox and authority receipts remain unchanged; no delivery state is fabricated or reset.
--   - Clinical dates and financial/report periods stay at their recorded values; use the manifest and guide date filters.
--   - Each database dump is internally consistent; there is no atomic PostgreSQL snapshot across all eight databases. Export after stopping writers.
--   - Restore requires empty isolated target databases and stopped applications; this file contains no DROP or cleanup procedure.
--
